What is EC2 Auto Scaling?
EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adds or removes EC2 instances in your group based on demand, cost, or health.

          It helps you:
                        Maintain application availability
                        Scale up or down automatically
                        Save costs by running only required instances
Prerequisites
          You must have:
          A Launch Template or Launch Configuration
          An EC2 AMI ready (Amazon Machine Image)
          Security Group & Key Pair
          VPC with subnets

STEP-BY-STEP: Set up EC2 Auto Scaling
          Step 1:     Create a Launch Template
                      Go to EC2 Dashboard → Launch Templates
                      Click Create launch template
                      Fill in:
                      Name: my-auto-scale-template
                      AMI ID: Select an existing one (Amazon Linux / Windows)
                      Instance type: e.g., t2.micro
                      Key pair: Select existing or create one
                      Security group: Choose existing
                      Click Create launch template

Step 2: Create an Auto Scaling Group
        Go to EC2 Dashboard → Auto Scaling Groups
        Click Create Auto Scaling group
        Fill in:
        Name: e.g., my-asg
        Choose the Launch Template you just created
        Click Next


Step 3: Configure Network
        Choose your VPC
        Select Subnets (usually at least two in different AZs)
        Click Next


Step 4: Configure Group Size & Scaling Policies
        Desired capacity: How many instances you want initially
        Minimum capacity: Lowest number of instances (e.g., 1)
        Maximum capacity: Upper limit (e.g., 3 or 5)

Auto Scaling Policies:
        Choose:
        Target Tracking Scaling Policy (Recommended)
        E.g., Keep average CPU utilization at 50%
        OR:
        Step Scaling / Simple Scaling policies
        Click Next

Step 5: Health Check & Notifications (Optional)
        Health check type: EC2 or ELB
        You can configure SNS notifications for scaling events (optional)
        Click Next

Step 6: Add Tags (Optional)
        Tags help with cost allocation and organization. e.g.,        
        Name = AutoScaleEC2
        Click Next → Review → Create Auto Scaling Group

Step 7: Attach Load Balancer (Optional but Recommended)
        You can create or attach an Application Load Balancer (ALB) so that traffic is balanced between all instances in the ASG.

Final Result
        AWS Auto Scaling Group will now:
        Monitor CPU (or other metrics)
        Add new EC2 instances when needed
        Terminate unneeded EC2s during low traffic
        Replace unhealthy instances automatically

Test the Auto Scaling
You can:
Manually increase CPU load using stress tools (for Linux)
Watch if Auto Scaling launches a new instance
Reduce load and see if it scales in (terminates instances)

🧹 Clean Up (Important to Avoid Charges)
Delete the Auto Scaling Group

Delete Launch Template

Delete ELB (if created)

